# NetFRAME Packet C: the agents the Wazuh manager is EXPECTED to have.
#
# This list is the authority, not the manager's registration list: an agent that is missing has to
# be noticed, and an agent nobody expected has to be noticed too. Never generate it from whoever
# happens to be connected. Change it by review when the estate changes.
#
# required  yes = its absence is a fault; no = shown as INFO only (a workstation that may be off).
# auth      journald = its sshd authentication successes reach Wazuh through the journal and are
#           checked for freshness; none = not checked.
# canary    yes = the monitor logs in as `monitor` from Jarvis (192.168.10.31) every cycle, so a
#           healthy system-journal reader always has a recent "Accepted publickey for monitor"
#           alert (measured 192-769 per host per 24 h, largest gap about 15 min).
#           no = no such login exists (pve1 is not a monitored node; Jarvis is checked locally).
# auth_h    freshness threshold in hours: 2 with the canary, 24 without it.
id|name|required|auth|canary|auth_h|notes
000|azuh|yes|journald|yes|2|the manager itself (Active/Local)
001|pve1|yes|journald|no|24|standalone Proxmox host, not a monitored node
002|pve3|yes|journald|yes|2|
003|Randy|yes|journald|yes|2|
004|pve2|yes|journald|yes|2|
005|QuarkyLab|yes|journald|yes|2|
006|pve5|yes|journald|yes|2|
007|pve4|yes|journald|yes|2|
008|Jarvis|yes|journald|no|24|the collector runs locally on Jarvis, so no monitor login
009|quixote|no|none|no|0|Windows workstation, may be off
